Who
KING’S UNIVERSITY, BANGLADESH (KUB) is a proposed non profit private university founded by Professor Dr Mohammad Abdul Hannan and led by an experienced Board of Trustees composed of educationists, professionals, and public service leaders.

What
KUB is a higher education institution offering undergraduate and postgraduate programs through the School of Business, School of Social Sciences and Humanities, and School of Engineering. It operates on a credit based system with English as the medium of instruction and maintains a strong faculty student ratio to ensure academic quality.

Where
KUB is located in Dhaka, Bangladesh. Academic activities are planned at a 25,000 square feet temporary campus in Mohammadpur, with a permanent campus under development at Sunvalley Abashon, Dhaka.

When
Established in 2025, KUB is currently in the proposed stage and progressing through the formal approval process in compliance with national higher education regulations.

Why
KUB was founded to provide elite, research driven, and ethically grounded higher education. It aims to develop future leaders, professionals, and innovators who contribute to national development and global advancement.

How
The university operates under a charitable trust model, with a secured Reserve Fund deposited in a scheduled bank to ensure financial sustainability. It reinvests institutional resources into academic development, infrastructure growth, and quality assurance.
